            <ArticleTitle>Measuring our natural painkiller.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-8; discussion 69</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Studies of the brain during noxious experience converge on the anterior cingulate cortex as a key region in the processing of pain. A recent exciting study extends this understanding to include the anterior cingulate as a center for endogenous opioid activation specific to negative pain affect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
